### SkillProof API Tests
### Use REST Client extension in VSCode to run these tests independently.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### 1. Register a new user
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "student"
}

###

### 2. Login user
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

@token = {{loginUser.response.body.token}}

### 3. Get Auth User
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth
x-auth-token: {{token}}

###

### 4. Add a Skill
# @name addSkill
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: application/json
x-auth-token: {{token}}

{
  "name": "React.js",
  "level": "Beginner"
}

###

@skillId = {{addSkill.response.body._id}}

### 5. Get Skills
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
x-auth-token: {{token}}

###

### 6. Add Evidence (Project) -> Should boost score by 15
POST {{baseUrl}}/evidence
Content-Type: application/json
x-auth-token: {{token}}

{
  "skillId": "{{skillId}}",
  "type": "project",
  "title": "E-commerce App",
  "description": "Built with React and Node",
  "url": "https://github.com/test/ecommerce"
}

###

### 7. Add Evidence (Quiz) -> Should boost score by 20
POST {{baseUrl}}/evidence
Content-Type: application/json
x-auth-token: {{token}}

{
  "skillId": "{{skillId}}",
  "type": "quiz",
  "title": "Advanced React Concepts",
  "score": 90
}

###

### 8. Get Evidence for Skill
GET {{baseUrl}}/evidence/skill/{{skillId}}
x-auth-token: {{token}}
